                <pb facs="0499" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg433"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Annex 4]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Draft Suggestion C Handed by the Secretary of State to
                        the Japanese Ambassador on May 16, 1941</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center">V. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Economic Activity of Both
                        Nations in the Southwestern Pacific Area</hi></p>
                <p>On the pledged basis of guarantee that Japanese activity and American activity in
                    the Southwestern Pacific area shall be carried <pb facs="0500" n="434"
                        xml:id="pg434"/> on by peaceful means, the Japanese Government and the
                    Government of the United States agree to cooperate each with the other toward
                    ensuring on the basis of equality of opportunity equal access by Japan and by
                    the United States to supplies of natural resources (such as oil, rubber, tin,
                    nickel) which each country needs for the safeguarding and development of its own
                    economy.</p>
            </div>
